## 3. Restrictions on Use

Users of SpectralBot are strictly prohibited from:

### 3.1 Malicious Modifications

- Modifying, altering, or manipulating the source code with the intention of introducing malicious functionality.
- Modifying the software to compromise the security, stability, or integrity of other systems or services.
- Using SpectralBot as a foundation, framework, or component for malicious software or activities.

### 3.2 Commercial Use

- Selling, licensing, sublicensing, or otherwise commercially exploiting SpectralBot or its source code.
- Using SpectralBot or derivative works for direct or indirect financial gain without explicit written authorization from the copyright holder.

### 3.3 Discord Server Abuse

- Using SpectralBot's `!force` commands to raid, disrupt, damage, or otherwise interfere with Discord servers.
- Using any SpectralBot functionality to facilitate harassment, unauthorized disruption, or malicious activity against Discord communities.
- Intentionally causing damage to Discord servers, their members, or their infrastructure through the software.

The `!force` functionality is provided strictly for legitimate administrative and moderation purposes. It is highly encourage to either delete the section, comment it out, or not use it altogether. Keep in mind that the default code files forward back to my Discord account (username 0_tida), so not editing the file would also mean that I would get authorisation to use the !force commands across all servers that SpectralBot is in. Editing the file beforehand to limit or remove functionality of the !force commands is highly encouraged.

Abuse of this functionality is prohibited, regardless of intent or claimed authorization.

### 3.4 Misrepresentation

- Knowingly distributing false or misleading information about SpectralBot, its functionality, capabilities, development, or official status.
- Falsely claiming to be the original developer, copyright holder, or an authorized representative of SpectralBot.

This restriction does not prohibit honest criticism, opinions, or factual discussion of the project.

### 3.5 Manipulation and Misuse

- Using SpectralBot as a tool to deceive, manipulate, coerce, or otherwise exploit individuals.
- Using the software to facilitate deceptive practices or interfere with the autonomy of other users.

